# =============================================================================
# PUBLIC REPO - DENY BY DEFAULT.
#
# This repo is a build output. Its only source of truth is the private
# ItJustFitzAI repo, synced via `python scripts/publish-site.py --apply`.
#
# Everything is ignored except the explicit allowlist at the bottom. If you add
# a file to the site, add it to BOTH this allowlist and DEPLOY_FILES in
# publish-site.py - otherwise it will not deploy.
#
# The point of deny-by-default: a stray copy of a business plan, a session log,
# or a docs/ folder cannot be committed here by accident. It has to be
# un-ignored deliberately.
# =============================================================================

# Ignore everything...
/*

# ...then re-allow exactly the deployable site.
!/index.html
!/dashboard.html
!/portal.html
!/robots.txt
!/sitemap.xml

!/assets/
/assets/*
!/assets/app-config.js
!/assets/puzzle.js
!/assets/ItJustFitzIconV3_No_Text-round.webp
!/assets/chatbot-puzzle-icon.webp

# Repo furniture that lives only here (not synced from the source repo).
# Cloudflare Pages needs no in-repo domain file - the custom domain is bound in
# the Pages project and served from Cloudflare DNS. CNAME was the GitHub Pages
# mechanism and is deliberately gone; _headers and _redirects are Cloudflare's
# equivalents and are pre-allowed here so they can be added without a second edit.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/_headers
!/_redirects

# Never, under any circumstances.
.env
*.env
.env.*
*.docx
*.doc
